Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Keep the window surface of client surface windows on Android.

Proton drops the window surface of windows with OpenGL or Vulkan client
surfaces. On Android the client surface is a view below the window's own
view, so without a window surface the last frame of it stays on top and
hides the rendering. Keep it; the server already clips the client area
out of it.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -2108,6 +2108,11 @@
     win_rect = win->rects.window;
     release_win_ptr( win );
 
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+    /* Android client surfaces are views under the window's own view, so the window surface
+     * must stay to draw the non-client area and leave the client area transparent */
+    ret = FALSE;
+#endif
     if (ret) return !force_present_to_surface( &win_rect );
 
     return ret;
